  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Mechanised army built around the LAV 6 and Leopard 2, with light battalions for Arctic and air-mobile tasks. Leads the NATO Multinational Brigade Latvia (Canada's largest overseas commitment). Experience from Kandahar (2006-2011) and training/advise missions in Iraq (Op IMPACT) and for Ukraine (Op UNIFIER).",
    "squad_size": 8,
    "fireteam": "Section of 8-10 split into two assault groups with a C9/C6 gun group; the LAV crew (3) provides fire support when mounted.",
    "tactics": [
      "Mounted advance in LAV 6 with the 25 mm providing overwatch, dismount for the assault",
      "Leopard 2 tanks lead in open terrain, infantry clears built-up areas",
      "Assault groups bound in pairs; C9/C6 gun group anchors the base of fire",
      "Cold-weather and Arctic patrolling (Canadian Rangers as guides)",
      "Careful IED-aware route discipline learned in Kandahar"
    ],
